.\" Man page for snif-conn, the SNIF connector wrapper.
.\" Keep in sync with the bin/snif-conn script and the connector variables in
.\" etc/snif.conf.
.TH SNIF\-CONN 1 "2026-07-05" "snif 1.03" "SNIF Manual"
.SH NAME
snif\-conn \- run the SNIF connector from /etc/snif/snif.conf
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snif\-conn
.br
.B snif\-conn \-d
.br
.B snif\-conn \-q
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snif\-conn
is a small wrapper that runs
.BR snifd (8)
in its connector role using the configuration in
.IR /etc/snif/snif.conf .
It gives a device a publicly trusted HTTPS hostname without exposing its private
key: on first run it allocates a permanent SNIF hostname and obtains a
certificate; thereafter it renews that certificate and, in daemon mode, forwards
the configured ports through a SNIF relay.
.PP
Run without arguments,
.B snif\-conn
initializes the connector and prints the allocated hostname. If the certificate
directory is owned by another user, it re\-executes itself via
.B sudo
as
.I SNIF_USER
so the certificate can be written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Run the SNIF connector daemon, forwarding the port map in
.IR SNIF_CONN_PORTS .
.TP
.B \-q
Quiet: suppress informational notices and the warning printed when the
certificate file is not writable.
.PP
With no option,
.B snif\-conn
performs a one\-shot initialization and prints the hostname.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The following variables are read from
.IR /etc/snif/snif.conf .
.TP
.I SNIF_CONN_CRT\fR, \fISNIF_CONN_KEY
Certificate and private key paths
.RB ( snifd
.BR \-c / \-k ).
.TP
.I SNIF_CONN_INITURL
CA\-proxy initialization URL
.RB ( snifd
.BR \-a ).
.TP
.I SNIF_CONN_KEYALGO
Optional key algorithm
.RB ( snifd
.BR \-K ).
.TP
.I SNIF_CONN_HOSTNAME
Optional fixed hostname
.RB ( snifd
.BR \-r );
must match the wildcard certificate.
.TP
.I SNIF_CONN_HOSTNAME_PORTABLE
When set (and no fixed hostname), request a portable pseudo\-random hostname
.RB ( snifd
.BR \-P ).
.TP
.I SNIF_CONN_PORTS
Space\-separated forward map used in daemon mode; see
.BR snifd (8)
"PORT MAPPING".
.TP
.I SNIF_CONN_DIR\fR, \fISNIF_USER
Base directory for the certificate and the user to
.B sudo
to when creating it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/snif/snif.conf
Connector configuration.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns
.B 1
if the SNIF directory is missing or a privileged re\-exec fails; otherwise the
exit status of
.BR snifd (8).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snifd (8),
.BR snifdog (8)
.PP
SNIF home page and live demo:
.IR https://snif.host
